course: dictionary
lesson: 6075
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Mess can be a thing or an action, and its meaning depends on the words around it. «You help tidy up any mess you made before you go home.» Here a mess is a place or things that are untidy or dirty, so you clean it up.
explain: Mess can also mean a bad or confusing situation. «I messed up my sum, so I'll start again.» Messed up means got it wrong, and the sentence tells you mistakes can be fixed. Check by swapping in your meaning: "I got it wrong, so I'll start again" makes sense.
explain: Small words after mess change the meaning. Mess about or mess around means to play in a silly way instead of working, as in «stop messing about». Mess with means to touch or change something you should not, as in «Don't mess with matches, plugs or medicines». Always check the little word that comes after mess.
fact: Mess can be a noun (a mess) or a verb (to mess).
fact: «Mess» means a place or things that are untidy or dirty.
fact: «Mess up» means to make something untidy, spoil it or get it wrong.
fact: «Mess about» and «mess around» mean to play in a silly way instead of working.
fact: «Mess with» means to touch or change something you should not. Never mess with matches, plugs or medicines.
exercise: «You help tidy up any mess you made before you go home.» What is a mess here? | A hard test | A kind of food | *Things that are untidy or dirty | A game played with a ball
exercise: «I messed up my sum, so I'll start again.» What does messed up mean? | Sang it loudly | Finished it very quickly | *Got it wrong | Made it neat and perfect
exercise: «Stop messing about» is said to a child who is playing silly instead of working. What does messing about mean? | Cleaning the classroom | *Playing or behaving silly instead of working | Counting to ten | Reading a book quietly
test: «Don't mess with matches, plugs or medicines.» What does mess with mean here? | *Touch or change them when you should not | Tidy them up carefully | Count how many there are | Play with them in a silly way
test: Which phrase means a bad or confusing situation with problems? | Mess with | Tidy up | Mess about | *In a mess
exam: Ella says, «What a mess!» The room is full of socks and crumbs. What does mess mean? | A dark room | Very fun | Very quiet | *Untidy or dirty
